Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm/gem: add modparam to disable shrinker blocking

Normally if we are under enough memory pressure, the shrinker will
eventually start waiting for BOs to become idle.  In some very latency
sensitive use-cases this is undesirable.

BACKPORT from the freedreno list, "[PATCH 2/2] drm/msm/gem: Add modparam to
disable shrinker blocking", Rob Clark, 2026-09-03:
https://www.mail-archive.com/freedreno@lists.freedesktop.org/msg46776.html

Left at the upstream default (true), i.e. no behaviour change on boot.  The
point is to expose the knob: a game hitting memory pressure would rather
drop a frame's worth of reclaim than block the submit path.  Flip it with
msm.eviction_can_block=0 or via /sys/module/msm/parameters/.

---

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_gem_shrinker.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_gem_shrinker.c
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_gem_shrinker.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_gem_shrinker.c
@@ -19,6 +19,10 @@
 MODULE_PARM_DESC(enable_eviction, "Enable swappable GEM buffers");
 module_param(enable_eviction, bool, 0600);
 
+static bool eviction_can_block = true;
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(eviction_can_block, "Allow the shrinker to block waiting for BOs to become idle");
+module_param(eviction_can_block, bool, 0600);
+
 static bool can_swap(void)
 {
 	return enable_eviction && get_nr_swap_pages() > 0;
@@ -26,6 +30,9 @@
 
 static bool can_block(struct shrink_control *sc)
 {
+	if (!eviction_can_block)
+		return false;
+
 	return (sc->gfp_mask & __GFP_DIRECT_RECLAIM) ||
 	       (current_is_kswapd() && (sc->gfp_mask & __GFP_KSWAPD_RECLAIM));
 }
